From d39138dcdcdddbf73eaa500a977f6af92b4389be Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sam Day <me@samcday.com>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 22:01:36 +1000
Subject: [PATCH] freedreno/a3xx: flush HLSQ before indirect const loads

Indirect const loads can wedge A306/FD307, unless an HLSQ_FLUSH or
CP_WAIT_FOR_IDLE directly precedes them.

A minimal reproducer was derived from GSK. In this case, there must be
a previous draw call in the submit, which can be anything (there just
has to be a previous draw). If the second draw performs an indirect
vertex const load, then a direct fragment const load, then the following
indirect fragment const load will hang.

However, SuperTuxKart causes it with an indirect vertex const load. A
minimal reproducer hasn't been derived here, so the preconditions for
the hang aren't as precisely defined as in the GSK case.

The characteristics of the hang are that CP ME stays busy, whilst RBBM
reports HLSQ, PC, VFD and VPC busy, until hangcheck recovery.

fd3_emit_state() is already emitting HLSQ_FLUSH before all constant
uploads, though interestingly it has a TODO indicating that maybe this
should not be the case.

Issuing the HLSQ_FLUSH between vertex and fragment loads does not
help. It has to be immediately before the indirect const load.

In lieu of a more precise target, fd3_emit_const_bo() is updated to emit
HLSQ_FLUSH before *all* const indirect loads. Many of these loads don't
need this guard. A slightly slower GPU is better than a hanging GPU,
right? Of course if someone can pin this down further that would be
great.

drm/msm emits an HLSQ_FLUSH at the end of a3xx_submit, which is why
FD_MESA_DEBUG=flush would mask the issue.

This fix was tested on both db410c with a 7.3-rc3 kernel, and samsung-a5
with a 6.12 kernel.

Closes: https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/mesa/mesa/-/issues/12634
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Sam Day <me@samcday.com>
---
 src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/a3xx/fd3_emit.c | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/a3xx/fd3_emit.c b/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/a3xx/fd3_emit.c
index 69a5368ac99..875a8e55a1d 100644
--- a/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/a3xx/fd3_emit.c
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/a3xx/fd3_emit.c
@@ -72,6 +72,11 @@ fd3_emit_const_bo(struct fd_ringbuffer *ring,
 
    emit_const_asserts(v, regid, sizedwords);
 
+   /* indirect const loads can wedge the FD307, when following other const
+      loads, unless HLSQ is flushed first. mesa#12634 */
+   OUT_PKT3(ring, CP_EVENT_WRITE, 1);
+   OUT_RING(ring, HLSQ_FLUSH);
+
    OUT_PKT3(ring, CP_LOAD_STATE, 2);
    OUT_RING(ring, CP_LOAD_STATE_0_DST_OFF(dst_off) |
                      CP_LOAD_STATE_0_STATE_SRC(SS_INDIRECT) |
-- 
